urn out  however democrat and former secretary of  state ross miller said on twitter in  several tweets  that he is positive he won the race he  tweeted several times in the past week  including this one here  saying that he is thankful for the  outpouring of support rest assured i  have won  this election and here at the top he had  worked alongside the county attorney  here in clark county for many years  he basically says that i know her legal  opinion is just wrong as part of the  legal machinations in all of this the  question is whether there will be a  special election for commission district  c and right now that is still very much  up in the air nevada republicans though  used that county commission report to  file a fifth  lawsuit against this election cycle once  again alleging widespread voter fraud  it joins a list of others filed despite  no evidence of widespread voter fraud  orkomana breaks down this latest legal  challenge  we are asking the court to recognize the  fact  that president trump was victorious in  this election  contesting the election results that's  the goal of the trump campaign's latest  lawsuit filed tuesday afternoon in  carson city district court but final  numbers show joe biden beat president  trump by nearly 35 thousand votes in  nevada the legal challenge largely  includes allegations we've heard before  including that more than 15 thousand  people voted both in nevada  and another state voters who are listed  as dead voted  and the signature verification machine  in clark county was not reliable this  all comes back to the unsubstantiated  claim that nevada's expanded mail-in  voting system resulted in irregularities  we had a lot of improper ballots being  mailed to people's homes and apartment  buildings  nevada and clark county have created  this crisis reckless  unsolicited mail-in voting  has created this crisis the nevada  secretary of state who by the way  is a republican has consistently said  there is no evidence of