ng groups at 50 people  snhd is not recommending that large  gathering plans be approved at this time  although gatherings of 250 or less will  not be submitting plans for review snhd  recommends  limiting of gatherings to 50 or less  and it looks like that will be the case  for the next couple of weeks  this week governor sysolak said he would  soon make an announcement on any steps  that have to be taken but  no exact date was provided there was  also news this week of a vaccine being  95 percent effective  the i-team's vanessa murphy spoke with  alex azar about it he is the health and  human services secretary for the federal  government and  the head of president trump's covet 19  task force  mr secretary thank you so much for  joining us um  first let's start with the vaccine how  will it be distributed  and when could nevada start seeing it so  the vaccine will be distributed using  the normal distribution system that we  use in this country to put hundreds of  millions of doses of  whether it's flu vaccine measles vaccine  other childhood vaccines out  every year going to use the tried and  true systems that work every year for  this vaccine  also we will be distributing the  moderna vaccine if it is approved  through one of america's great wholesale  distributors and it will go  directly to wherever the state's  governor tells us  he or she would like vaccine to go  whether that's at a  retail pharmacy at a hospital a nursing  home  community health center or otherwise the  pfizer vaccine  again the governors will tell us where  they would like it to go  but we'll give them direction and pfizer  will ship it directly to that site  where we will match up that vaccine with  the kits that we have put together with  the needles the syringes the personal  protective equipment  to enable that vaccination to occur  ballpark  date could you provide um and also  in a state of about 3 million like  nevada how much would we initially get  well in terms of timing it's going to  depend first the companies have to apply  for authorization  before the fda pfizer has said publicly  that they expect to file within the next  couple of days i would hope that  modernity would get their application in  soon also  at that point the fda will run its  rigorous process to review all of the  data  safety and efficacy information they'll  run a public advisory committee process  to consider that information with an  independent body  once fda has granted authorization to a  vaccine  our colleagues on operation warp speed  from uh the defense department have said  that they believe they could have it  shipped out and received  within 24 hours we have also said  that we will be distributing the vaccine  which of course will be  in limited supply initially on a per  capita basis  across the country so nevada will get  its proportional  amount of vaccine based on nevada's  population compared to other states  it's no secret governor sisilek and  president trump have  clashed what would you say to people who  think politics could affect this or  people who may not trust the trump  administration  or the vaccine in that it moved so fast  well politics has and will play no role  whatsoever  in the consideration development or  approval of our therapeutics or vaccines  there are over five separate steps in  independent checks in the process  whether it's an independent data and  safety monitoring board which has  reviewed this data  to enable the company to see it the  company's own independent ethical checks  to ensure that they want to submit an  application  the fda's publicly published guidance of  what standards they will hold it to  the public independent advisory  committee that will consider  the vaccine application and then finally  the fact that it will be fda's career  scientists  who will make the determination to  approve and authorize a vaccine  politics have no place in in this type  of public health of therapeutics and  vaccines  alex azar speaking with vanessa murphy  there for now groups like  health care workers and nursing home  residents could get the vaccine  in december dr anthony fauci from the  national institutes of health says every  day that american everyday americans  rather  can be vaccinated as soon as april next  on politics now policing the police  if there are bad cops out there i don't  want them standing next to me out there  in the community  how metro police's use of force policy  has changed and who investigates claims  against the department  also raising money for education the  hurdle passed by two ballot initiatives  that would raise taxes for our schools  coming up next


